rdks.mail - e-mail utilities
----------------------------

at the moment it contains two modules and one BIG CLI program!

modules:

  * outlook:  deals with the (annoying) Thread-Index header.
    - utils.parse_thread_index:  CLI for the outlook module.
        (run with: `python -m rdks.mail.utils.parse_thread_index`
         or simply `parse-thread-index`)

  * content:  deals with RFC 1521/2045 content transfer encodings
              (currently only the encoders are implemented).

program!

  * compose.py:  composes RFC 5322 e-mails with MIME version 1.0
                 (depends an awful lot of on python's RFC 5322
                  style-preserving header parsing & creation,
                  though MIME body encoding comes out of the box. :)

installation is a bit harder due to compose.py depending on
rdks.list, but this should work:

    git clone https://git.rapidcow.org/rdks-mail.git
    # depending on where your python/pip3 command lives
    # you MAY have to change pip into pip3, python -m pip, etc...
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    pip install -e ./rdks-mail

(of course you could clone rdks-list too and... but i think you
 already know how to do that)

remote version (XXX: NOT tested)

    pip install -r https://git.rapidcow.org/rdks-mail/plain/requirements.txt
    pip install git+https://git.rapidcow.org/rdks-mail.git

license is GPLv3+, that plus is doing work because it means
you are explicitly allowed to "upgrade" to a newer version.
see COPYING for the full license.

